  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "important": true,
  "source": "NEET 2025",
  "question": "A photon and an electron (mass $m$) have the same energy $E$. The ratio ($\\lambda_{\\text{photon}}/\\lambda_{\\text{electron}}$) of their de Broglie wavelengths is: ($c$ is the speed of light)",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\dfrac{E}{2m}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$c\\sqrt{2mE}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$c\\sqrt{\\dfrac{2m}{E}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{c}\\sqrt{\\dfrac{E}{2m}}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Photon: $\\lambda_{\\text{photon}} = \\dfrac{hc}{E}$. Electron: $\\lambda_{\\text{electron}} = \\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{2mE}}$.\n\n$$\\frac{\\lambda_{\\text{photon}}}{\\lambda_{\\text{electron}}} = \\frac{hc/E}{h/\\sqrt{2mE}} = \\frac{c\\sqrt{2mE}}{E} = c\\sqrt{\\frac{2m}{E}}$$",
  "solution_diagram": "",
  "status": "published",
  "updated": "2026-09-25"
}
